WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.480
Avengers: Infinity War is a game-changer for
the Marvel Cinematic Universe, and the movie's

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.910
post-credits scene is crucial to a complete
understanding of its cliffhanger ending.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.150
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the end-credits

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.550
scene to reveal what it means, easter eggs
and how it sets up Avengers 4.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.960
I'm also kicking off a new Avengers giveaway,
so make sure you're a subscriber and leave

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.900
a comment about the movie to enter.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.210
As you'd expect, spoilers ahead for Avengers:
Infinity War.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.170
The post-credits scene starts with Nick Fury
and Maria Hill driving through New York.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.690
Fury asks Hill if there's any word from Tony
Stark, but although Hill is monitoring satellites

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.590
worldwide, she's not picking anything up as
Stark's on Titan.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:47.059
Hill does get a signal though for multiple
unidentified crafts over Wakanda that have

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:51.980
an energy signature 10 times those seen during
the Chitauri invasion of New York.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.339
Fury then mentions a name which sounds like
Klein or Clint but he gets cut off as a car

00:00:56.339 --> 00:00:58.679
swerves out of control in front of them.

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:03.249
As Hill and Fury check the car that crashed,
they find the driver's seat is empty because

00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:04.839
the driver has disintegrated.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:10.500
A helicopter then smashes into a Manhattan
skyscraper, again because the pilot has vanished;

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.330
and Fury tells Hill to "Call Control.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.330
Code Red."

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:19.530
But Maria Hill starts to fade into ash and
people in the street also start to disappear.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.860
Fury runs to his car, grabs a device and as
he activates it, he also starts to evaporate

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:24.990
into dust.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:29.400
The device falls to the ground but blinks
a message "Sending" for a few seconds before

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.770
coming up with Captain Marvel's emblem.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.850
So, this is a pretty crucial scene as it shows
the Snap event that Thanos initiated is already

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:38.990
happening on a global level.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.270
At the end of the movie, we saw the Snap wipe
out around half of the heroes assembled in

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:47.930
Wakanda and on Titan, but this extra scene
shows that it's now a wider event with Thanos

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.490
fulfilling his goal of wiping out half of
all living beings in the cosmos.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.750
This is a pretty desperate situation and,
on the surface, it seems a rather bleak ending

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.610
to the movie, however, that final shot of
Captain Marvel's logo brings a much-needed

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.860
ray of hope.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.630
The introduction of Captain Marvel will be
essential to how our surviving heroes will

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.860
try to take down Thanos in Avengers 4.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:13.600
Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin Feige has
said that Captain Marvel will be the most

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.250
"powerful […] character [that Marvel] has
ever put in a movie.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.240
Her powers are off the charts, and when she's
introduced, she will be by far the strongest

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.270
character we've ever had."

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:26.790
Before she arrives in Avengers 4 though, Captain
Marvel, played by Brie Larson, will be debuting

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.770
as Carol Danvers in her own solo movie where
we'll get to see exactly why she's so important

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:33.319
in the MCU.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.740
Danvers first appeared in Marvel Comics in
1968 and obtained her powers when during an

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.050
accident her DNA bonded with that of Mar-vell,
a Kree alien.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.750
Carol Danvers has an incredible variety of
powers ranging from superhuman strength, to

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:50.930
space flight, plus energy absorption and projection
among others.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.900
Brie Larson has said that Captain Marvel is
"a believer in truth and justice and she is

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.300
a bridge […] between Earth and Space".

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.450
And that means she's key to fixing the ending
of Avengers: Infinity War where there are

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.490
just two surviving groups of heroes.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:08.160
In Wakanda, we've got Captain America, Black
Widow, Bruce Banner, War Machine, Rocket Racoon,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.069
Okoye and M'Baku and on Titan there's just
Iron Man and Nebula.

00:03:12.069 --> 00:03:17.080
As for Shuri, Wong and Pepper Potts, their
fate during the snap event is, for the moment,

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.080
unknown.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.209
For Avengers 4, the heroes who are separated
will need to band together and I can see that

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:26.910
Carol Danvers being a bridge between Earth
and Space could be able to make this happen.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.930
By the way, it's interesting that the movie
begins and ends with a distress signal: at

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.650
the start, it was the Asgardians under attack
from Thanos, and now, it's Fury to Captain

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:36.650
Marvel.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.450
Regards to Nick Fury, it's obviously pretty
heart-breaking to see both him and Maria Hill

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.540
just fade to ash in this scene, but it's a
really striking way of showing the universal

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.500
and devastating effect of Thanos's snap.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.700
That moment is made even more poignant coming,
as it does, in a film that celebrates the

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:57.450
tenth anniversary of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, because, after all, it was Nick

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.770
Fury who appeared in the very first Marvel
Studios post-credits scene at the end of Iron

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:03.770
Man.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.150
"'I am Iron Man.'

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:08.210
You think you're the only superhero in the
world?"

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:11.480
"Mr. Stark, you've become part of a bigger
universe."

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.819
"You just don't know it yet."

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.519
"Who the hell are you?"

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:18.639
"Nick Fury, Director of S.H.I.E.L.D."

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:19.639
"Ah."

00:04:19.639 --> 00:04:23.180
"I'm here to talk to you about the Avenger
Initiative."

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.270
Actor Samuel L. Jackson has been cast in the
Captain Marvel movie which will also explore

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.430
Fury's origins and very likely what led him
to the Avenger Initiative.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:36.110
It's set in the 1990s where we'll meet Nick
Fury at a time before he lost an eye.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:40.050
Talking about Fury's role in the film, Kevin
Feige has said that Fury "has reached a point

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:44.300
in his career where he thought the Cold War
is over and the best days are behind him.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.789
And when he encounters certain things in this
movie, it sets him on a path that leads us

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:51.650
to where we are 19 films later."

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:56.120
Looking at the device Fury used to contact
Danvers, I thought it seemed a bit dated in

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.439
terms of tech, which made me suspect it may
have been designed in the 90s and so it's

00:05:00.439 --> 00:05:03.690
quite possible we'll see it in the Captain
Marvel movie.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.599
Another possible hat-tip in the post-credits
scene is to a moment in Captain America: The

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:08.889
Winter Soldier.

00:05:08.889 --> 00:05:11.490
Spoiler ahead if you haven't seen The Winter
Soldier.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:15.710
In that movie, Fury had to silently spell
out a message to Steve Rogers to let him know

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.729
that SHIELD had been compromised.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:22.979
In both films, Fury is warning another superhero
of a threat and, just as he does, the former

00:05:22.979 --> 00:05:24.740
SHIELD director is killed.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:28.349
Or at least, he appeared to die in The Winter
Soldier, because later it's revealed that

00:05:28.349 --> 00:05:30.080
the death was a fake-out.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.789
And I suspect that Fury's death in this post-credits
scene could well be reversed in Avengers 4.

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:39.260
Something that will need to be addressed in
the Captain Marvel movie is why Nick Fury

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:42.169
never contacted Carol Danvers until now for
help.

00:05:42.169 --> 00:05:46.340
After all, there have been some global-threat-level
events, like the Chitauri invasion of New

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:50.479
York in the first Avengers film, and then
there were the events in Sokovia in Age of

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:51.539
Ultron.

00:05:51.539 --> 00:05:55.800
It's possible that, as serious as those incidents
were, Fury felt comfortable enough that the

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.990
Avengers could contain those threats.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:03.029
However, in Infinity War, the threat is clearly
massively larger with Maria Hill saying the

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:07.270
energy signatures of the invaders over Wakanda
were 10 times bigger than those recorded during

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:08.960
the Battle of New York.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:14.409
With Tony Stark unavailable and people literally
vanishing around Fury, it's likely that all

00:06:14.409 --> 00:06:18.370
this is why Fury hit that Captain Marvel distress
call now.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:23.029
By the way, Nick Fury's "MotherF.." was, of
course, a joke about Samuel L. Jackson's signature

00:06:23.029 --> 00:06:28.449
curse word and him finally getting to almost
say it in the MCU, but I wonder if it's also

00:06:28.449 --> 00:06:32.379
a little wink to Age of Ultron when Fury scolds
Cap about his language?

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:34.229
"She's dusty, but she'll do."

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:36.449
"Fury, you son of a bitch."

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:37.449
"Ooh!

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:38.800
You kiss your mother with that mouth?"

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:43.190
We also need to talk about the name Fury drops
just before the car crashes in front of him

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.539
and Maria Hill.

00:06:44.539 --> 00:06:49.409
Fury's line isn't totally clear and sounds
a bit like he's saying "tell Clint" meaning

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:52.820
that he's trying to get in touch with Clint
Barton, aka Hawkeye.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:58.680
But, if you listen really carefully, he actually
says "tell Klein to meet" just before he gets

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.849
cut off.

00:06:59.849 --> 00:07:04.539
Klein refers to Cameron Klein, the former
SHIELD tech who refused to launch the Insight

00:07:04.539 --> 00:07:07.569
helicarriers in Captain America: The Winter
Soldier.

00:07:07.569 --> 00:07:11.879
Klein also had a brief cameo in Age of Ultron
where Hill and Fury saved him from one of

00:07:11.879 --> 00:07:13.330
Ultron's bots.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:18.099
Interestingly, in the comics, Klein has worked
alongside Captain America and his grandfather

00:07:18.099 --> 00:07:20.460
was saved by Cap during World War Two.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.599
And I wonder whether Klein's name drop in
the post-credits means we'll see this tech

00:07:24.599 --> 00:07:29.140
specialist reappear in Avengers 4 to help
the Avengers pick up the pieces of the snap

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.930
aftermath?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.449
Another little thing to look out for in this
scene is the model of the car Hill and Fury

00:07:34.449 --> 00:07:35.449
are driving.

00:07:35.449 --> 00:07:39.639
Suitably enough, it's a Nissan Infiniti [QX50]
which has already featured in an Infinity

00:07:39.639 --> 00:07:41.129
War-related promo.

00:07:41.129 --> 00:07:45.490
Now, you may still have a lot of questions
about how the snap and Infinity War's cliffhanger

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.539
ending is going to be resolved, and I go into
lots more detail about that in my ending explained

00:07:50.539 --> 00:07:51.539
video.

00:07:51.539 --> 00:07:55.169
I'll add a link to tap here and in the video
description below as soon as that's live.

00:07:55.169 --> 00:07:59.580
So, what are your thoughts on the end-credits
scene and the Captain Marvel tease?

